 sounds like accompanying, not union.  {lo}expressions are also sets in the=
 same sense.  If {lo'i} means something else, it means C-sets, which are vi=
rtually useless for linguistic purposes and belong, if at all, to MEX. =20
> In passing, I note {me} being used for "is a member of", which is not wha=
